    <id>https://doi.org/10.1177/10422587261485969</id>
    <title>How Can We Research Social Mobility in Entrepreneurship?</title>
    <updated>2026-09-28T00:00:00+00:00</updated>
    <author>
      <name>Elsa T. Chan, Steven A. Brieger, Ngoc Luu, Marii Paskov, Mirela Xheneti</name>
    </author>
    <content>&lt;b&gt;Entrepreneurship Theory and Practice&lt;/b&gt; &lt;br&gt;Social mobility is a central concern in contemporary societies, yet its dynamics within entrepreneurship remain insufficiently understood. This paper’s purpose is to facilitate research on entrepreneurial social mobility by making three key contributions: first, we examine the distinct conceptual and methodological challenges related to capturing social mobility in entrepreneurship and provide strategies for solving them; second, we introduce multidimensional social mobility measures that move beyond the predominant focus on income-based metrics in existing quantitative research; third, we demonstrate how alternative quantitative and qualitative methods can produce more holistic evidence for understanding social mobility among entrepreneurs.</content>
